@meeting train.m6.calder
// Pillar 5, M6 making it safe (Day 8, Monday ~10:30): your first incident, a burst pipe in the junior wing. Calder
// meets you at the Works bay door. Short: it's urgent. Head writer, seat W.
title: Burst pipe
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder showed you how to handle an incident: make it safe, clean up, then fix the cause. Always in that order.
== lines
calder: Burst pipe. Junior wing. With me.   [gesture]
calder > you: Three steps. Safe. Clean. Fix. Never in another order.
calder: Safe means shut it off upstream. Follow the pipe back from the wet.
calder: Nobody's hurt. Nobody will be. Walk, don't run.
calder: Go.
